 "verdict": "COHORT: cohort intact: all 6 declared checkpoints measured SEED STABILITY: across-seed sd of pooled diversity is [4.093, 11.443, 11.906, 7.574, 10.252, 9.867] against means [7.5, 26.25, 31.5, 185.125, 205.125, 196.125]. In the low-diversity cells (mean < 60) the sd averages 9.1 against a within-dip span of 24.0, a ratio of 0.38. The single-seed values F111 used deviate from these means by up to 30%. RECOMPUTED PRIMARY: with seed-averaged diversity, rho(diversity, lambda_ca) = +0.771 with a bootstrap 95% CI of [+0.714, +0.829] over 4000 resamples. F111 reported +0.943 from single draws. pooled diversity across checkpoints spans 197.6 against its own noise floor 3.249 (60.83x, gate 2.0x) F111's motivating observation SURVIVES re-grounding: the correlation holds with seed averaging and its CI excludes zero, so the single-seed values were noisy but not misleading. BOUNDARY: one family, one temperature, one radius. This re-grounds F111's premise and does not re-test its conclusion; the dissociation grid averaged 3 seeds x 16 replicas per cell and is untouched by this.",
